    q: "How do you save and deploy an ML model?",
    level: 'Advanced',
    a: "After training I save the whole pipeline (preprocessing plus model) with joblib so I load exactly the same thing in production. Then I serve it behind an API, for example a FastAPI endpoint that validates input with Pydantic and returns the prediction, and package it in Docker. I also log model version, inputs and predictions for monitoring.",
    code: "import joblib, os, tempfile\nfrom sklearn.datasets import load_iris\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n\nX, y = load_iris(return_X_y=True)\npipe = make_pipeline(StandardScaler(), LogisticRegression()).fit(X, y)\n\npath = os.path.join(tempfile.mkdtemp(), \"model.joblib\")\njoblib.dump(pipe, path)                      # save\nloaded = joblib.load(path)                   # load in the API server\n\n# In FastAPI: @app.post(\"/predict\") -> loaded.predict([features])\nsample = [[5.1, 3.5, 1.4, 0.2]]\nprint(\"Loaded model predicts:\", loaded.predict(sample).tolist())\nprint(\"Same as original:\", (loaded.predict(X) == pipe.predict(X)).all())",
